he general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ y &=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{20}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-0.71$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $3.54$ | $0$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/94/9446137440c19f9aca73c9c666089ecff5a7712ee3f389ab891a150c13ffa780.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)|\\le 1$ and $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)|\\le 1.$ Thus, the obtained curve is $\\text{bounded}.$ So, we have $\\text{an ellipse}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/06/0678458809cf39967d7dda0d1ffbe4d43541ec309266bd08da6245ec23f6439d.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57cb91e2-e7c9-5578-af8d-fe8d65375825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305998} {:answer/id #uuid "84c88ee5-8339-54bf-a8c1-c9f2b55b031d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "phase portrait" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306417} {:answer/id #uuid "dce64447-b543-5dbc-89b6-04657d7d6d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "phase portrait" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306417} :answer-field/id #uu