ype/math} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306530} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5b02e9-894e-547b-9287-21f51b1c9c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306530} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef595f89-fcc5-504f-b52d-d0ce5b92dd38" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03729fe4-1fcd-555f-b5aa-aa039dc0b034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305184} {:answer/id #uuid "18c07006-aa66-5b01-b4bc-9b102a6b053b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305377} {:answer/id #uuid "791a84bd-f4ac-50f8-806b-0f330b00c84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306306} {:answer/id #uuid "996df7c2-18a9-5086-8369-f7a34b950157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306584} {:answer/id #uuid "de71b9d2-f2b9-5f9c-b36e-768a947d69e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306306} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8439c53-ab6f-5a4c-9fbb-ad4d33f688a1" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308309}] :question/id #uuid "507d4f13-d348-5702-be62-c98bacbf5b02" :question/math-academy-id "q-333756" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=-2\\pm 5\\text{i},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1,2}=[\\pm \\text{i},1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={{field-1}} \\\\ y &={{field-2}}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{20}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.52$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.52$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/18/18f4793f4f1edc907e28b0e148510dd3c8131a544fb703d91d0a1feb0cd8a4d1.png)\n\nAs $t\\to \\infty ,$ the curve\n{{field-5}}.\nSo, we have\n{{field-6}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-7}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-8}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe {{field-9}} of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/c0/c001f8a99c09e3d1da8c6107a298989c03e64ec58c23319ce0837a757c5ddafd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={e}^{-2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ y &={e}^{-2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{20}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.52$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.52$ | $0.53$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/2b/2b273edc4f977f2bee4d9a8c41128d4f2071ec39b0840610cbb7ee44492aae3e.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)|\\le 1,$ $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)|\\le 1,$ and ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, the curve $\\text{converges}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we have $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nAgain, since ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/c0/c001f8a99c09e3d1da8c6107a298989c03e64ec58c23319ce0837a757c5ddafd.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2647e169-3dc0-54c7-8b4c-60518680dd89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426996} {:answer/id #uuid "33860977-2245-503b-93c1-924abfe8e5e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427005} {:answer/id #uuid "b0771a33-629d-5128-bab8-7a2e8fe0910e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427059} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d44bd7-7c26-5418-b34e-2d6a9d002bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427065} :answer-field/id #uuid "005c8a3e-ea06-5428-9cc5-7969138abf4d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4d551b-4426-59d3-98b5-7ebee569edea" :answer/type {:db/ident 