mplex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty ,$ we require $a>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64d15c0d-286c-5db2-a374-6e5e4f0ca2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427023} {:answer/id #uuid "8f04802d-784a-549b-887a-7dbd17012ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427042} {:answer/id #uuid "d5edc49b-5842-5c9b-9513-948fbbfb2d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427042} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c69f5bf-d740-5156-847f-22b4ebc71f50" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f7e6e7-a4af-53d6-b2a6-013b0b02b813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426986} {:answer/id #u