id "0c9a66a9-5063-59bb-a558-35f241023ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351671} {:answer/id #uuid "272ea8e4-eb66-5aad-8dbf-fa964cee63b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351923} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb0ccf2-5cff-57b2-893b-9df01aa2e1d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352686} {:answer/id #uuid "8acfb015-f9b8-5b02-bbe6-7889f38f07d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352778} {:answer/id #uuid "c65a0a83-605f-520b-ba29-92d7ee96d718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351671} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1012b5-8fab-5e26-8a2e-4dc74c827b47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354022}] :question/id #uuid "5b9b4918-d355-5d49-9319-d404a4197395" :question/math-academy-id "q-85170" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{15-12}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ -27\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354400 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11dba67a-a53a-58f2-89c8-9df640fc96e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351717} {:answer/id #uuid "a09c3159-033f-55ff-9b7d-add980e5704e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352941} {:answer/id #uuid "af86ad1e-6b56-5530-98e8-12967904063f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353061} {:answer/id #uuid "b587df15-5a45-5878-bf8f-9973b97719fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353120} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f68496-8f75-5793-86d4-499cab4c6109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352941} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e3b5067-2ea8-5cb1-80a2-4797f4faa983" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354023}] :question/id #uuid "b177e082-aca8-5ae3-bb5e-4b8f9e1549ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-85171" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{18-16}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6e33f13-bf32-57fc-9e33-1c3365d2b549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389018} {:answer/id #uuid "45edddc3-4ab5-5f20-b063-71b14cfab775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389019} {:answer/id #uuid "a609d06b-6fba-58d1-ac0c-77b3c30ee67f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389020} {:answer/id #uuid "27df9d1e-2610-5e00-b40d-bca3d5157238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389021} {:answer/id #uuid "428468dc-0f82-5095-b6bf-387fc8aa1e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389022} :answer-field/id #uuid "991862b1-972b-5127-a2c8-a89e2bc72fa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389017}] :question/id #uuid "ede69c8f-2758-5c85-a62b-6b678eca588f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159976" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-6-(-4)}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092071 :question/id #uuid "7969785b-fc71-50f4-9d73-da5599630b6e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5467" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](images/7b/7b8cdc56144f73cd1e3510c155508478767d0bf058e854e39f52bcad0f2e0413.png)\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle $S'$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ The triangle $S'$ has vertices $(4,3),(4,10),$ and $(-4,-3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(1,0)$\n\n- $(4,-3)$\n\n- $(-1,0)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of $S'\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n![](images/e7/e7f7558d370d506a87ea9466703f9f9ac2e4ea970572b67c06d2114cdbc0f6fa.png)\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by $T^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4-(-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 28 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(1,0),(2,4),(-1,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8387023f-37c7-58e6-b9f8-b928291b1811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091571} {:answer/id #uuid "93069ae0-78c7-5ae6-836d-e53a506a2fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091572} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3ac131-fb45-5994-b624-86bc22526145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091573} {:answer/id #uuid "eea359f0-cc8a-56f3-acf9-d369258dee62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091574} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3a3cdb-c7e9-5fd9-b097-39dabfafb380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091575}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4c2d86b3-e5bb-559c-a488-28d0c525e53b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091570}] :question/id #uuid "4fe0ec10-c00f-5a52-823c-2c275473fad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-9259" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle $S^{′}$ under the action of $T$. The triangle $S^{′}$ has vertices $(2, 0), (-3, 3)$, and $(0, 0)$. Which of the following are vertices of $S$?\n\n1. $(0, 2)$\n2. $(1, 1)$\n3. $(0, 0)$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc493c0-81df-5623-a6e9-9c5a16b69477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460383} {:answer/id #uuid "918c5786-5f57-563e-87e4-a3f4c9aa6a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460383} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e3afd7-70f3-5443-a940-a339bbad0965" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96010fcb-b968-5cc9-9c1d-22d751cc5f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460385} {:answer/id #uuid "17db0d5a-8a60-5321-9b61-7b407ba1f35c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460385} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef13f0c4-fe8b-5269-baef-59f689061648" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df1c8590-d9f8-544c-a5ba-79c864300fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460387} {:answer/id #uuid "6c914876-7b74-55b4-b5b4-42cfba24c2d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460388} :answer-field/id #uuid "caaf4985-b97e-5199-82ce-87fd88a2e02a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461060}] :question/id #uuid "867b7546-7038-557a-b857-b13076be50c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-9265" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(0,2),(-3,3),(12,4),$ and $(7,3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(-2,2)$\n- **II.** $(1,-1)$\n- **III.** $(4,4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -6 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 8 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,2),(-3,3),(4,4),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eacbb59-a929-525c-9777-e78ce8861ec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234765} :answer-field/id #uuid "209a10fb-8572-5f53-95ba-ac4784ed4be6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235003} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32bc3241-fc63-5c3b-a7eb-826fdc50e457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234626} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cb97038-8f24-5744-a235-9626db1c46e7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09fd7968-d30a-5288-990c-bd8929494325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234560} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb0d748f-d37d-5e1b-8361-da6e2a938817" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235273}] :question/id #uuid "93171830-13e5-5388-8d32-35a485ad8695" :question/math-academy-id "q-138786" :question/problem "A triangular recreational area next to the housing complex is mapped to a larger recreational area under the action of $T.$ The larger recreational area has vertices ${L}^{′}(-15,4),$ ${M}^{′}(-15,2),$ and ${N}^{′}(-21,6).$ Find the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of the larger recreational area:\n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)(-3)-0}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 15 & 21 \\\\ 18 & 24 & 24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertices of the smaller recreational area are $L(5,6),$ $M(5,8),$ and $N(7,8).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f05073e6-bfb4-5b8d-8db4-310e7dfa5a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461881} {:answer/id #uuid "f8cc566f-6c98-5ea4-b7be-dc39ac81a01d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461881} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5f69b8e-f7c4-5e0a-9f1d-00394a46cc6a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04970681-2afb-550f-9388-bd0cba68f0a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461883} {:answer/id #uuid "2edff474-152a-55c0-91ad-ecc28535f220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461883} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa044452-e56e-5ba8-a718-24f5a020ad8c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5254f4e8-74dd-5cce-a282-1148360c51fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461885} {:answer/id #uuid "f5978d27-0a47-584a-877f-15e8629c4892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461886} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdc29db2-90c6-5990-862a-26c63df63336" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462696}] :question/id #uuid "9d13de60-db83-5fa3-ae76-e5805b3d5848" :question/math-academy-id "q-11974" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,-2),(-3,2),(2,2),$ and $(-1,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n- **I.** $(2,2)$\n- **II.** $(0,1)$\n- **III.** $(-5,-8)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-(-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(0,-2),(-5,-8),(0,2),(0,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256707 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6f8e547-af48-5682-8cb8-9735daf137fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462049} {:answer/id #uuid "1ffc3df7-935b-55dd-898a-b4f350700906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462050} :answer-field/id #uuid "08918d95-147b-5c17-964b-fbe4a402aafb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8fe2f28-234b-5195-8ae3-225b9a029355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462051} {:answer/id #uuid "cb77398c-765e-5328-adf2-825b0fb48082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462052} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6e515d-ee91-5f57-acdb-689c1e4bb6e0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4bdccb-4a6b-5a80-884c-094072e98a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462053} {:answer/id #uuid "fb248762-0e83-5bcd-b409-3390e810d66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462054} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2c67c05-2f48-5fdf-8d8e-3bb13e3688a9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462780}] :question/id #uuid "d8bbd25c-a5f8-5d3d-a21d-9b7c851329bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-12273" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(2,-5),(3,-6),(4,-8),$ and $(3,-7).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n- **I.** $(-5,-2)$\n- **II.** $(-6,-3)$\n- **III.** $(-8,-4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0-(-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -6 & -8 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(-5,-2),(-6,-3),(-8,-4),(-7,-3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a6fe8d-2c16-5ed9-a469-12e945598a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462055} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c56ce9-c0a0-567a-8fb9-6d9dd256d42a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462056} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb39bce1-60cf-5bba-9192-7ca5348113b4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc0dd62-2bc3-5a3e-aafc-1436ace1cfcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462057} {:answer/id #uuid "1e0886d8-9672-5eac-953d-670d4c428f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462057} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0eec58b-6298-53fe-96fc-caaa73418a7e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "697c2615-8e40-5e82-9789-3f41e7c39420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462059} {:answer/id #uuid "367997cf-efbe-5ae7-8cd3-8c02764c0897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462060} :answer-field/id #uuid "95cfd858-94a4-5845-a230-50e26ead8ca0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462783}] :question/id #uuid "566b96ca-03b3-52b8-9e22-e29d835f5f92" :question/math-academy-id "q-12275" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(0,4),(-4,4),(12,4),$ and $(7,3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n- **I.** $(-2,4)$\n- **II.** $(1,-2)$\n- **III.** $(4,4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -8 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(-2,4),(-4,4),(4,4),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7101408f-83b0-53a4-9d55-00c45a966c4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464642} {:answer/id #uuid "f7356944-1eaa-575e-ac04-b539110561d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464642} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f86394-110c-5718-9e3e-4d3a9d8f1867" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71effc6a-8fc8-50ec-86b9-8f98c88a6abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464644} {:answer/id #uuid "828cb3b4-314e-55ec-9768-fd99e9fe5a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464645} :answer-field/id #uuid "839660db-3166-5987-a542-4fa490d95abd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232d9374-233d-5629-956a-e36cf8001e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464646} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb62c8a-d11d-5783-88d9-54c022383db9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464646} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce970b0a-25ab-5978-bd72-be88cbe19226" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465257}] :question/id #uuid "13406d62-3495-5617-8c59-07fc2d20bdc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-159977" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(3,4),(0,2),$ and $(7,10).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(0,1)$\n- **II.** $(2,3)$\n- **III.** $(1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4-2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(1,1),(-1,2),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b2f177c-7c21-5975-af01-918dbb607f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464648} {:answer/id #uuid "a252e595-5423-567f-8ed6-fc3437b74bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464649} :answer-field/id #uuid "336c7955-c71a-5099-ad3c-06d88308b4f9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465258} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a7a2a8-7048-50dc-b42e-17c2bbc49e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464650} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8f7889-e691-5daf-8746-8108b5e441ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464651} :answer-field/id #uuid "b894feb5-b122-57cd-95b3-21387ac16c77" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e9869bf-8d59-5052-bd07-f073613a107e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464652} {:answer/id #uuid "fd781cda-d7c3-5695-b89c-3ca178e7c968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464652} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f9da67-714c-5e27-8823-83d168cc53a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465260}] :question/id #uuid "b0b402cc-9d61-5ea9-b280-42fd73163096" :question/math-academy-id "q-159978" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(3,2),(7,5),$ and $(2,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(-2,2)$\n- **II.** $(1,1)$\n- **III.** $(0,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{9-8}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(1,0),(1,1),(-2,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60aeceb2-c5da-5e6b-8673-013a7ce9f253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469416} {:answer/id #uuid "0631cdb5-cf4c-53b0-b966-c2db161ca9bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469416} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ec5c65-abca-5e17-a2b9-802dbf8092af" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b12a98e-82ff-5582-9ca1-f5f41faf9607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469418} {:answer/id #uuid "9bdb6d8f-6dfa-532b-8456-42a0532caa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469419} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd3ac97-c9b9-59d3-8e3b-cc1e1916883d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72b45d09-71fd-57e6-85ea-fb403eef9129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469420} {:answer/id #uuid "c82aa0b5-8204-50ec-adc5-f5a9ef7a76f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469421} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb4780d0-a59e-5e3a-82a2-83cbded54cbe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470322}] :question/id #uuid "9ca71fc4-780f-59ae-bb16-2f59cfd2fbb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-85172" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(10,5),(0,-5),$ and $(15,20).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(9,5)$\n- **II.** $(0,1)$\n- **III.** $(10,-7)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{35-30}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 50 & -125 \\\\ 5 & -35 & 95\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 10 & -25 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 19\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(0,1),(10,-7),(-25,19).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b68ce632-6e8f-57d4-b15f-d3f5f26f9e02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469578} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6e0fda-efae-56fd-bb3d-c94a991faf92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469579} :answer-field/id #uuid "df23e6e6-a55c-54e2-84c5-3e8b3b8e7be2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470401} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6339a41a-de7b-5f72-bb5f-2cbd7c5ae565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469580} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc89e1b-573c-5ee0-910b-05fb7a358af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469581} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a003f5-318e-5c98-8b44-a32c95fbf50e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d3017b-7ead-58ef-b9a2-bc9f8cf94b2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469582} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3ea1c2-3ca2-588d-adaa-b40a57de928e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469582} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed1ef14-e5f2-5b10-aa8a-4ea6c00242de" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470403}] :question/id #uuid "0704d357-8cb1-56bb-b120-20ad34cf98ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-9253" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(-1,0),(1,0),$ and $(0,1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(1,0)$\n- **II.** $(-1,0)$\n- **III.** $(0,2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2-0}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(1,0),(-1,0),(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357522 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5517a81-c0eb-5943-8e2a-9c8a54bf8eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469584} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c8d0af-1691-5009-b5cb-1348ab0791eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469584} :answer-field/id #uuid "0678ee0a-5861-53f8-ac37-366434415f44" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470404} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b0ff69b-7651-57fe-bdbe-d2db6aa50855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469586} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdd79a4-e36d-5fc1-bc93-f702b063009b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469586} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3f6ce4-5cce-54ed-b535-7e4c84063cdf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af74279b-63b5-5d79-8259-57fc9b29a647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469588} {:answer/id #uuid "422d0615-7052-5247-8065-184d37fec22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469589} :answer-field/id #uuid "c39184ad-8688-52c6-80fc-34cdcfa71132" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470406}] :question/id #uuid "da6f4133-24dc-5140-aaa0-0ea075dfe3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-9255" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(3,2),(14,6),$ and $(9,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(3,2)$\n- **II.** $(1,1)$\n- **III.** $(5,1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357523 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c350a3-1b79-58a9-a807-6ab58e5c39d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469590} {:answer/id #uuid "459d147b-5230-51a3-b435-5764d57b48f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469590} :answer-field/id #uuid "62763c2c-39ef-5712-adcd-826c341a7d5d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29bf996a-d223-5d8b-b569-ef8fd06bbda0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469592} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4dda13-b642-5253-91e2-cb13e9240b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469593} :answer-field/id #uuid "647bb206-3e1d-5257-85fe-c96790b2eaf0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470408} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a48dcd7-a11c-52c1-a562-dffc4bd7358a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469594} {:answer/id #uuid "2b454448-bf22-5948-adc1-80b7a802d3cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469595} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14bec1d-5e8a-5bf0-8d68-2cfd98cefed0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470409}] :question/id #uuid "1174578d-6631-5fcf-81bf-729c1fac3da6" :question/math-academy-id "q-9258" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(4,-1),(17,-3),$ and $(10,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(3,2)$\n- **II.** $(-1,1)$\n- **III.** $(5,1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-0}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77b25b30-e0bb-5259-9539-cf0d164d3467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469596} {:answer/id #uuid "eabf8157-2e6a-5210-bbcc-06fd9c4f3272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469597} :answer-field/id #uuid "28ae18bd-3280-53d5-9fcd-448d879f7c0a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8cf7fa1-e149-501b-b2e3-3ed65df17e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469598} {:answer/id #uuid "f7782d42-4cf1-52c7-89d6-678892697267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469598} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb5831cf-9d5a-55f3-87f8-440f5b3f12f1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470411} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "943d2282-2316-5feb-80f1-ef274b9b6334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469600} {:answer/id #uuid "ea36bc5d-0f0b-5664-ad09-08540fc57ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469600} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eccf71b-1fb1-55b0-9102-1181a0c2354c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470412}] :question/id #uuid "5f585952-0c84-59bf-89fe-d6813830d204" :question/math-academy-id "q-9260" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(-21,0),(21,0),$ and $(0,3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n- **I.** $(0,-3)$\n- **II.** $(3,1)$\n- **III.** $(-3,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-7-0}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-3,0),(3,0),(0,-3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2157482-a1ed-5c32-91c2-2cab3e0b29c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469602} {:answer/id #uuid "08825dbb-0967-5083-b253-6d569886e119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469602} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c6eef7-bb20-50b1-8491-d122c6f76acb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470413} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9a0cab-5103-5fd4-a52b-50ea7da02210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469604} {:answer/id #uuid "89a83d76-34ee-597b-9f18-1f25448cd531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469605} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4f4803-022c-5e61-ad7c-fd87835ca2ac" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470414} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a37a48a-62bd-5f94-ba3f-582c40aa535a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469606} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce845a9-4e70-5f8f-a138-471f6fb70668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469606} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b30972c-bbe2-55b7-a495-cbd625baa16f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470415}] :question/id #uuid "a755a352-feaa-5539-8e01-5e0ad683e5ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-9261" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,2),(-5,4),(-3,2),$ and $(0,0).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(-2,1)$\n- **II.** $(0,0)$\n- **III.** $(2,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3-2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,2),(-1,2),(-1,0),(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3307adb3-5e7b-5a1c-b154-e424b9a8cce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469608} {:answer/id #uuid "16e994d5-8aca-50cd-b782-685a035d4e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469608} :answer-field/id #uuid "98432bd3-be83-56c5-be17-ef5c3526b650" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a490851-61ea-542d-9ec2-ecbc61f04dd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469610} {:answer/id #uuid "11d75742-d0ed-5b85-9531-f012f15d5ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469611} :answer-field/id #uuid "20415130-a9ec-526d-b11a-edbb061373d9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470417} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86da18ef-3371-5b27-a2a4-337b78b73d79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469612} {:answer/id #uuid "ac7dfe73-a4ed-57e1-b5f5-9ef81bfa244a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469613} :answer-field/id #uuid "86423d97-11b1-595d-bf1a-f3d303cc250d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470418}] :question/id #uuid "c32a27cb-e2ec-5eaa-a1cb-1ea5655b2b83" :question/math-academy-id "q-9262" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(2,-5),(3,-6),(4,-8),$ and $(3,-7).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(1,3)$\n- **II.** $(3,3)$\n- **III.** $(2,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,2),(3,3),(4,4),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb8c9e9-6518-56b3-b761-1900dbfdc0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469614} {:answer/id #uuid "bd8782ff-f906-5f86-a2a5-645db754ee25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469614} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9eccc2b-e5fc-5020-9f8d-0d951b7e499f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f42b83be-71f8-5618-b28e-4b3841ab82e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469616} {:answer/id #uuid "aa78b7a0-5468-53c2-8d90-8778c853d3b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469617} :answer-field/id #uuid "86dfd80d-9ac3-57f4-a4c8-74ee1c428e3b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c940779-44b1-5051-ad77-677f0181ae8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469618} {:answer/id #uuid "d4214c92-7321-5cd8-ac94-77091ec48611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469618} :answer-field/id #uuid "96707c37-5356-5b94-8ecb-cbe01fa290a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470421}] :question/id #uuid "4a6a4708-c258-5b5f-8c4c-fa774844e5ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-9263" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(1,1),(0,0),(-1,1),$ and $(0,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(0,-1)$\n- **II.** $(1,1)$\n- **III.** $(-1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1-(-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2bc64c6-664a-5b24-aa66-f3eba12645eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469620} {:answer/id #uuid "c28bee52-3d67-53f6-ad56-642b64e05043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469621} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3824387-31bc-52a2-846e-2cd22ab4bb71" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d150ea-6336-53f3-9ff9-69a5bbd01ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469622} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad7216c-e3b7-5ed2-868b-6a0ea8df964a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469622} :answer-field/id #uuid "60197c06-01e3-5c67-9cf2-3b20020bd750" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470423} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d91462d4-c453-51f4-a051-ec052973b66e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469624} {:answer/id #uuid "4b540585-d54d-5c51-a990-620c2d48bdfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469624} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf37dfab-4b60-5bca-be75-986b98bb898e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470424}] :question/id #uuid "56746454-856c-5001-bcf8-93772c0debce" :question/math-academy-id "q-9264" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(0,0),(-2,-2),(-4,0),$ and $(-2,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(2,2)$\n- **II.** $(0,1)$\n- **III.** $(-2,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-1-1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,0),(2,0),(2,2),(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"}] :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106897} :activity/id #uuid "f9fd061e-b62c-59b3-95e7-cb70aa81601f" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106897 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107154 :tutorial/content "Consider the triangle below with vertices $(0,0),$ $(2,1)$ and $(2,3).$\n\n![](images/f7/f7c16deb083b467c063c900196274d08c532ad4633354f375530cb2cbe270491.png)\n\nWhat is the image of this triangle under the action of the transformation  $\\mathbf{T}$ represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all vertices of our triangle written as columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(0,0),$ $(2,0),$ $(2,0).$ Notice that these points lie on the same line. Two of them even coincide!\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$ is the following line segment:\n\n![](images/88/88383b8eca1805c158f80d998d844d4c666b15d118a0ec26b4a1ba43c781fc76.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\nThis is an example of a linear transformation that does not preserve linear independence. \n\n* First, notice that since [math]\\det(T)= 0,[/math] the matrix [math]T[/math] is singular, which means that the vectors represented by the columns of [math] T,[/math] given below, are *not* linearly independent. \n\\[\n\\left\\{ \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}, \\:  \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\right\\}\n\\]  \n\n- Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ and region $D,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\n \nSince $|\\det(T)|  = 0$ in this case, any object applied to $\\mathbf T$ collapses to an object with zero area.\n\n- Also, the fact that $|\\det(T)|  = 0$ tells us that $\\mathbf T$ has no inverse transformation. Therefore, it is impossible to recover the original triangle knowing only its image and the matrix $T.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "260cef8c-3f93-55cc-ac8c-258b2555991e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7693 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "91fe4680-2271-5bd9-a679-84fcae2b774c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106898}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106898 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6"} :step/id #uuid "1608691b-a3f7-54f4-82a1-b60b84369109" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106899}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106899 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105894 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747"} :step/id #uuid "cdca196d-b54e-5e0f-8148-f89ac24552f6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106901}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106900 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fea43b6-fd7b-5edc-b6b7-7f8b2cbab502"} :step/id #uuid "fe3d3d75-3555-5f42-96ec-0bc13603e728"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106901 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107155 :tutorial/content "Given a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with an associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ there are three possibilities regarding the type of object formed under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$ by a two-dimensional preimage. \n\nTo demonstrate, consider the three-sided polygon $\\mathcal P$ with vertices $(0,1)$, $(2,0)$ and $(2,1),$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/97/97689c7aaf7f6d42314fd01cb36b557df8081880659bcea08905e6c57f358ac1.png)\n\nLet's describe the three possible types of object formed by the image of $\\mathcal P{:}$\n\n- Case where $T$ is non-singular:\n\nLet $\\mathbf T$ be the linear transformation with the following matrix representation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can easily check that $T$ is non-singular by computing its determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $\\mathcal P$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\mathcal P$ and then compute the product $TX{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of $\\mathcal P$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$ is a triangle.\n\n![](images/14/145753e4f69dfa67bb45f59b7e9ed8bca789c589d4c5340ce2112363fa70cd7b.png)\n\n- Case where $\\mathbf{T}$ is singular and has at least one nonzero entry:\n\nLet $\\mathbf T$ be the linear transformation with the following matrix representation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can easily check that $T$ is singular by computing its determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the image of $\\mathcal P$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the image of $\\mathcal P$ under the action of  $\\mathbf{T}$ is a line segment.\n\n![](images/46/46d387dbf6678d324135dbbb3439688c0bdbf9f9567baef56f34aa4aa9ee22e3.png)\n\n- Case where $T$ is the zero matrix:\n\nLet $\\mathbf T$ be the linear transformation represented by the zero matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nClearly, $T$ is singular. Now, computing the image of $\\mathcal P$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are all $(0,0)$, the origin $O$ of the coordinate system. \n\n![](images/db/dbb9fce92da1f231a31e110f6cabb6faaf1bb43961a6c1de012c7c302c7af928.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "0bc95d9b-74ad-509c-8c28-e4e34606b376" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7702 :tutorial/title "Image Types Formed by Linear Transformations"} :step/id #uuid "c766a184-7dd4-51fc-8815-53eaecbc38c4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106902}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106902 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107156 :tutorial/content "In general, for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with associated $2 \\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $\\mathbf{T}$ is non-singular, i.e., $\\det(T) \\neq 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $\\mathbf{T}$ is singular, i.e., $\\det(T) = 0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system." :tutorial/id #uuid "593c9d77-3990-5aef-8f2f-1ef87dd41c59" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7708 :tutorial/title "A Summary of Image Types"} :step/id #uuid "b9b4bf14-bd02-5562-869e-62d28d1f3854" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106900}}] :activity/title "Singular Linear Transformations in the Plane" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105986}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186049254 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105460 :question/id #uuid "dcd503a8-a9c6-524b-a8ac-0641ce3e1107" :question/math-academy-id "e-12423" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](images/3f/3ff8dc37a532cfe49a2fbd8c02a1b27c50642d8e4c54def6984f3596f68065fa.png)\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,2), (0,1)$ and $(1,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of $S',$ the image of $S$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$\n\n- $(-2,0)$\n\n- $(0,0)$\n\n- $(2,0)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $S'$ are $(-2,0),$ $(0,0),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II,  and III.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e971391-4cb0-595b-bd98-df89dd35a4db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459711} {:answer/id #uuid "d2554c46-118b-50e6-81c2-e76e87db8349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459711} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff6dd613-a7fb-50b1-9a06-7f32416f198b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f18d124c-03b8-541d-922c-918788287861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459713} {:answer/id #uuid "372ec9f0-c827-52d6-bdcb-6bbbf1721a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459714} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eba0062-e828-5a75-aab1-f4f76c8bf3cd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f10aa70-6280-50ef-9adc-52b1dd5ac722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459715} {:answer/id #uuid "1e00dd01-9f54-5df7-80dd-b26feed7a988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459716} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf8e1c7a-a489-515c-8a07-8dd3a7d0ca1d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460724}] :question/id #uuid "0a22c71f-e8b7-5c07-9b29-38703fb5f2e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-21067" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(0,-1),$ and $(0,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(4,-1)$\n- **II.** $(0,0)$\n- **III.** $(-4,-8)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-8),$ $(-1,-2)$, and $(0,0).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d70c49cc-47a0-5157-b9e8-1a55f6a9d0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460473} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ebc32-6d79-5d58-bfb1-01412c4b840d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460474} :answer-field/id #uuid "c05c7404-e1f5-59ac-8224-db0b6e2cd44a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40bf32c8-3c87-58ba-9995-948cb586c6fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460475} {:answer/id #uuid "d98120ae-3c78-5a9f-afe8-13a7d12e3df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460476} :answer-field/id #uuid "c298a4be-cad1-5acb-83fe-f64df13fe125" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e31242f-1ccc-567c-b85d-6f4e22f24d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460477} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8ba8f6-b11f-5b8e-8aa8-ac18d8c7e850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460477} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46b6209-20d1-54b6-9102-6a18630bf5a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461105}] :question/id #uuid "cd611935-717e-54db-b36b-c834b2cac00c" :question/math-academy-id "q-96858" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,1)$, $(2,1)$ and $(1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-2,1)$\n- **II.** $(-8,4)$\n- **III.** $(3,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-8,4)$, $(-12,6)$ and $(-2,1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b3ae7d4-993f-5430-b747-8986186d90fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464336} {:answer/id #uuid "2869d7f3-1b96-5dd5-b0ee-6c3483909fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464337} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4fe13b9-b461-5404-b579-d68d54cca664" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc53e1ca-d2b5-5bf5-9f01-959fdb70deba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464338} {:answer/id #uuid "161f0366-48c8-5ba7-af35-ca8c9a24aa9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464339} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f506c58-26c9-5596-a8a5-1dd2c2a8a692" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d21af34-3afd-5f67-97ee-02ead5548978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464340} {:answer/id #uuid "95080681-e8e2-5196-9852-abd8418b6244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464340} :answer-field/id #uuid "06baf51a-09b9-58c1-8af9-5d0f7258e947" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465104}] :question/id #uuid "1d122f7d-248a-5adb-b7f8-d6731998c545" :question/math-academy-id "q-147666" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,3)$, $(-2,0)$ and $(2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(8,-16)$\n- **II.** $(-6,12)$\n- **III.** $(8,16)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1dc097f-1d45-5954-ab58-ae2d5d480624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464342} {:answer/id #uuid "7baca676-28e5-5fc3-a177-996e1ce40ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464343} :answer-field/id #uuid "85b6b509-5bca-5a90-a4c2-4fce1e466596" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "949bf759-caef-5f6e-8122-5b8ee2d18f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464344} {:answer/id #uuid "7359df24-8e1b-527f-88c9-aa439b96a42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464344} :answer-field/id #uuid "f82e39bc-0ba9-546e-8634-7c85456024dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc8121f-bbec-513b-a049-d0ed40f6ee68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464346} {:answer/id #uuid "1ada007f-92c5-599a-97cf-02ed61244306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464346} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d54219b-bc8a-5314-ba61-2881e9c259be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465107}] :question/id #uuid "1bd0a07c-db54-5589-8d88-4cb094a8efc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-147667" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(-1,2)$\n- **II.** $(-3,12)$\n- **III.** $(7,-12)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 12 & 2 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,12)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(7,-14).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04ca492-480a-5623-adc9-4e521cf13ef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464348} {:answer/id #uuid "4b473fab-557a-5736-821f-bef2379dfe95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464349} :answer-field/id #uuid "13691578-6cd6-5575-a669-641815258e64" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91a17bce-1fa8-5bcb-9c25-c1e4b2dc0f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464350} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6764bd-6c8b-5d43-800b-ef3990a25d18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464350} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7dd1d5c-287c-5541-8703-5173d2296e14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465109} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f50ae257-20c2-5968-97c3-5cbdffe94936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464352} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5fe2ec-892f-5374-91eb-d80cfa9e00e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464353} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8ee657-f121-51ff-9eea-9d96b2041f94" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465110}] :question/id #uuid "84cfa7aa-4b60-5511-b592-0b61d5c3575c" :question/math-academy-id "q-147668" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,0)$, $(0,-3)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(12,-24)$\n- **II.** $(8,16)$\n- **III.** $(2,-4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -24 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-4)$, $(12,-24)$ and $(-8,16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd338836-3b2b-5b26-8e4d-99852c2a9bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464354} {:answer/id #uuid "179235ad-f7f9-555b-aa29-ce74349a060b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464354} :answer-field/id #uuid "4851510e-ff1c-5dd3-9b4a-53d9daafba8f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4545c652-48fc-5b2e-b66f-24978de6015f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464356} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0519f2-65fd-5e40-9099-0de2ec98cdaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464357} :answer-field/id #uuid "f86ff3f0-dbd9-5649-a219-b88401932a40" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465112} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e2ec58-818b-58b2-891e-b5ed185c63b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464358} {:answer/id #uuid "f2050509-422d-5fd9-ba9d-ec9c3f