wer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464360} :answer-field/id #uuid "34227506-4938-5fe4-8dea-ec004383758d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2fecc27-b093-5c06-81b7-3f67926c503f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464362} {:answer/id #uuid "13c209d5-bfab-5979-a859-9614e3ef82d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464362} :answer-field/id #uuid "794e4752-0f94-5d57-aa3c-7cb714d5ea79" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acf09f49-4268-51ef-9f3f-ed7f146ff502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464364} {:answer/id #uuid "febf1aa2-4164-5237-86a0-d301e1357485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464365} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0dc0749-8a7d-54bf-bd14-a1ab81456b68" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465116}] :question/id #uuid "097bf1b0-31a1-5f77-a025-cb53554e53aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-147670" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(0,0)$ and $(2,2)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$  \n- **I.** $(6,-18)$\n- **II.** $(-5,-20)$\n- **III.** $(12,-24)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -24 & 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are  $(12,-24),(0,0)$ and $(-6,12).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f788cf-dc8b-5b55-ade8-a9c81ce81890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464366} {:answer/id #uuid "435566bf-2ec7-535d-aa0c-6761bce8c846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464366} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3754501-3237-584a-8a86-f0112c8cf28f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d827900-4ac5-5e1e-bc57-48dc0e654dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464368} {:answer/id #uuid "28303806-7d7f-566a-be92-43e668fa98d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464369} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1ddc9d-d7f1-5789-bdc0-d9f1be6f36fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "485755f2-6470-5593-a93f-71a7146656a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464370} {:answer/id #uuid "523298c8-b743-5311-aa0e-9312d5e0f3a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464371} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a0e2e3f-7761-580b-bf82-de8d40eb59b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465119}] :question/id #uuid "32f22262-a81f-543c-b306-489aa3da6008" :question/math-academy-id "q-147671" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(0,2),$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(6,-1)$\n- **II.** $(7,-14)$\n- **III.** $(8,-16)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 12 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(8,-16),$ $(-6,12)$, and $(7,-14).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #