th matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,2)$, $(-1,1)$ and $(3,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(12,6)$\n- **II.** $(4,2)$\n- **III.** $(4,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(12,6)$, $(4,2)$ and $(12,6).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0c5a18-5e11-5682-aee9-c5b1edaa8279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465839} {:answer/id #uuid "411a4d79-00d3-5b92-ac8a-3ec8a1e3f2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465840} :answer-field/id #uuid "9421c86b-2a6a-50f6-8512-cf27184b37ad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56f4be8b-4b7c-56a4-9398-01021eea2d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465841} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc9a459-35a8-5a20-9e97-123a79808c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465841} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd23d91b-7e49-54fe-974f-8f13e9c8eb9d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367a2d75-1ecd-5ed6-b56c-88c44b0b8e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465843} {:answer/id #uuid "79ca7384-4b46-5ca8-8121-1fb3ddfac730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465843} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcad1d36-8c15-56ba-96ea-8a418c029efc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466765}] :question/id #uuid "9622b4aa-6606-5dbb-91d5-63f920f6e03c" :question/math-academy-id "q-21068" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,2)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(-1,0)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(16,8)$\n- **II.** $(8,2)$\n- **III.** $(-4,4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$ \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(16,8)$, $(8,4)$ and $(-4,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93f1c390-0d52-5c61-8d8a-7a5fa63effe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469866} {:answer/id #uuid "c584a46f-a75a-5e89-be52-8bb669681c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469867} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9ef615a-b96a-5383-a0ac-041bb76125fb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470545} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e199f933-612f-5f8f-938b-a47f9346bb61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469868} {:answer/id #uuid "281a3b57-caf0-5ef9-9b67-0636b3cafd30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469868} :answer-field/id #uuid "661159f6-d76d-5337-a5ba-4b0c21ce9ae7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "609d3dc8-fb04-5b46-9d5c-0d04a9998ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469870} {:answer/id #uuid "22cf7953-1f96-59bb-b222-bec1a682923c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469870} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fd438fe-248f-5b63-a47f-ff64630e73bb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470547}] :question/id #uuid "e1d4a0e7-8ceb-5003-89cd-d540839fd74d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96855" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(10,20)$\n- **II.** $(4,-8)$\n- **III.** $(-6,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -4 & 10 \\\\ -12 & -8 & 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,-12)$, $(-4,-8)$ and $(10,20).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eab5693-da12-5573-98d2-914b3e12b5c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469872} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ff3136-e82c-5764-b831-f508f7cc961e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469872} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb591b12-5ddd-5b7c-b516-9d0afdb7ff88" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbaf6140-9e34-5ed5-b8da-cd3527d54932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469874} {:answer/id #uuid "8576213b-ae76-5796-845c-f78bcab64b1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469875} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cd78585-b14a-5ede-9aac-0fb6d8a76426" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9548e387-0612-50a6-b2ce-c8aaf16214c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469876} {:answer/id #uuid "83c5b7ff-cf0f-5896-93c9-7248c571fa9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469876} :answer-field/id #uuid "a525d91f-6d56-5631-8b8d-6244e6dc1297" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470550}] :question/id #uuid "0b46e610-7522-5441-8d91-b874b0e467ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-96856" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(1,1),$ and $(3,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-1,4)$\n- **II.** $(-2,4)$\n- **III.** $(1,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are  $(-2,4)$, and $(1,-2).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9849851-50ee-5f0d-ab89-ef7a2fc9f84c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469878} {:answer/id #uuid "733fd798-ea86-56ea-afb5-fb25093de365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469879} :answer-field/id #uuid "f23ba425-e844-50c7-9a2c-187594d0ae48" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49eb446a-3c97-5556-bf19-ea42b18fb478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469880} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a855ae-fa58-561d-83d1-244e26fd4609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469880} :answer-field/id #uuid "a564b121-378d-5751-91f3-38367384f6f0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92cb42d6-33e7-5895-a2ef-8224d17bd632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469882} {:answer/id #uuid "bde6ef7f-70fd-5236-a1cb-ae7873bad5de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469882} :answer-field/id #uuid "5757eb5a-153a-5404-853e-2408f7e8d9f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470553}] :question/id #uuid "ae6d946d-9a9f-5816-82c2-7048c4392f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-96857" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(-2,1),$ and $(3,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(1,3)$\n- **II.** $(0,-3)$\n- **III.** $(2,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-9),$  $(1,3)$, and $(3,9).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" I only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105894 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105461 :question/id #uuid "964efb4a-6e6b-5fc1-a993-20aa2b0acdaa" :question/math-academy-id "e-12424" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](images/54/5414050f8a5a5208b4424333e947919ce196687f8bfb0e60c2ced0a04a2695cc.png)  Find the image of the triangle shown below under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ \n\n![](images/85/853fd7d5c09944a5bacd0c2b3453504f3fa1eea9d8d3b2c3bdd4f0f44889dc16.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n![](images/95/95c80fe2654c8f6eb4b65492eab1efb07f568375b2960b1633e5e2e1a7741a8b.png)\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6), (1,-2),$ and $(-2,4).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/3f/3fd1073b2eaa5aa9c21e537fcc4dc6cf538ab2992c0732f64da50dbcb63d8fd4.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c96041d9-ce53-5436-89db-83f4961c78d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f4/f48ec1f750eff37beeb6b6110cd4b99f0d02d3ebb8f5fc73359f56f3a7b759fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289367} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3af17b-a8dd-5455-9359-7444f9120b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a3/a3b7fbc6ad805b72858f781916b6a2cd314647627109b3f6ba68025f7a9bf3be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289399} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cbad2b-25cd-521f-bc52-c8ca55f8c6d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a741d3518d7bb6194dbeec4ea327c5211067b4af5104deabf9b16694cbfba05.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289546} {:answer/id #uuid "e514598a-3418-5dd7-b0af-c0f266918a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/01/0108d7abfdebeb9b2bb1ac3c3bb84e7ee0d8caeedb3ebc341ca540413abce0b0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289550} {:answer/id #uuid "f5387913-e99d-5991-befe-2bdbcd3cae6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289649} :answer-field/id #uuid "62794a91-3170-5db9-a768-6bfc2b4e78f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289940}] :question/id #uuid "87f1b1b7-4122-5900-82fa-45ed68940b46" :question/math-academy-id "q-21061" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/2f/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e898be8-84be-5cb3-8edf-9122089194ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0aa81715b158f7fef5556c2f1054f67b4e9a21a4451cfcee649fbc99c31da651.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358017} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb1c4d1-593d-5b51-a062-bb3192959e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e316ceff92e78155ee352a2e5c3c526d30852fb1803fd9cfb938bea3e5cf984.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358029} {:answer/id #uuid "2d3a6dc9-8fdd-5c70-9b0d-fd85269b6239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c1/c1cd5cc238c79e5de9a5830d539deb91f8da6b38e01aeb3f8349fff661740da0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358157} {:answer/id #uuid "46e17cca-31e6-5b30-a2de-28aa4873d997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6ba878568654dc85dba3ac561617132f851e62b63473eb8239fa716f53cd0dcd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358363} {:answer/id #uuid "9ded4668-3a77-5e6d-bc14-2fac29066177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70a89dff7f615f258e6f5ab33f9eaa302d48882b5e11deb0253a8b8ee0237865.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e316ceff92e78155ee352a2e5c3c526d30852fb1803fd9cfb938bea3e5cf984.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358029} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc5b111-6e04-59f2-8c1f-6661132b0541" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360175}] :question/id #uuid "e654df3b-ce22-5258-85fb-03604192e335" :question/math-academy-id "q-96873" :question/problem "![](images/13/131d9f30fac5b1cc4b8eb72a989ca16b0d3cbf7d16725aa38581bfd115b1fc77.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,-2)$, $(-1,2),$ $(-4,8).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/87/87d2a7f522d68e1a50d9c5bb5e33498b2a28e869785f5109c4f6bf3a1c7ff701.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f02789c-570a-5a55-9668-ccecf796280b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6b0143a0adc22d1834fc404c9da0d03b2143c8cbc16a29a9286637920694002d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272926} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8812c0-3ce7-5a3e-821b-1c5c2ffb4913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc6d39b05ae4862121b7b76b555be7b19931eda478e84973181e74e8d628db2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273472} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ef2660-487f-5f0e-96ad-72d13af828d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f5be8864e70a021eb2fa717a9a7998c645e3792a68d23de54a07114b7a566cf1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274243} {:answer/id #uuid "e56c5810-fb99-5d8a-8b9c-cf22cebf22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/130f215103a0c955d14ac386a382afae09c22f507491bc54a408ad13a154cbc5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274414} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c42471-c98a-5fa9-8652-78bb7d90ce52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1faae8b1750b1c402f88ef801cd6609d259c37c523ac4bf4a7cb795034a9bd1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1faae8b1750b1c402f88ef801cd6609d259c37c523ac4bf4a7cb795034a9bd1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274532} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fde73a2-4951-547f-b50c-7da51291c95b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274719}] :question/id #uuid "e6736730-8ce9-58a7-80ed-e4390a0dad27" :question/math-academy-id "q-147523" :question/problem "![](images/77/771f1ffeda2b0041e1485611315661eed0bc88a601513d4fd4b2088022521aa8.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,2)$, $(1,-1)$,  and $(-2,2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line. \n\n![](images/e1/e1faae8b1750b1c402f88ef801cd6609d259c37c523ac4bf4a7cb795034a9bd1.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a86d12-69d9-56a1-817e-d4968620eead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b6fe02d5b3d96aeaa6a4edc9a027ec69993330252322e10a57618dd499bb02b5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272717} {:answer/id #uuid "600fe537-8139-54e6-8499-1048f26a0109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/df/dfa05a8c2c943d5f74e5e5fef468006117c97b2d3d0a7b7a6b9c2024b6089272.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273212} {:answer/id #uuid "971e62f7-bcdf-5aa4-9d15-a67fb6f22937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e316ceff92e78155ee352a2e5c3c526d30852fb1803fd9cfb938bea3e5cf984.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273693} {:answer/id #uuid "b43bb04d-93d1-5c23-8383-65a16ea74d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6ba878568654dc85dba3ac561617132f851e62b63473eb8239fa716f53cd0dcd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273949} {:answer/id #uuid "dcedc36c-f8b2-5ab5-91bc-01e989bdf542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d3f815e4205f0a24a125162072843fe507d0683ce40a89fdd13ee29c296f7500.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b6fe02d5b3d96aeaa6a4edc9a027ec69993330252322e10a57618dd499bb02b5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272717} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa20c628-0334-54a2-9235-4c0e4958e73d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274935}] :question/id #uuid "b4143bfe-8679-54ed-be74-9249bee7dc11" :question/math-academy-id "q-147605" :question/problem "![](images/ad/add078cb1b05f772f25c91a4736f5aacd4490ff8556ce6a0d0ea7ad44869d0e7.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 10 & 0 & -20\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,10)$, $(0,0),$ $(4,-20).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/8c/8c86cb108725b3f1c7b5731dda0f11a5cb21a7daa023c5153cce1ece3ba6ba0f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0161ff6a-e88e-5667-9f0e-5d0932fcb766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f9040d78661e0d33290ad14e1ddf815211985f5963c8e1c8b9b5438dd8f3931c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272394} {:answer/id #uuid "537b50a5-d7d2-5fb2-a567-227056701261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/69e3e6eabe9e2ea5d28a6ff0feb40437965649af45ad247b572a35ac3bf642a4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273099} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0dfe60-0b4d-5b6c-8884-eee6d217a9cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d271c5f4cf0f250dcfdbba8addfdc5f8c583832f378756fc3066e2b961a31dc3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273335} {:answer/id #uuid "79d116da-1281-5a37-8986-c47c8248233a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d38c8f370e25add2a06ecc652127bae817e2c8bc394f4db6fdf539fbfef3750c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273435} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd25416-a091-553b-9e7c-7ce1eb127ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274180} :answer-field/id #uuid "5234edc3-074b-52c1-a5f9-b3e5983c93d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274772}] :question/id #uuid "49259d02-2f18-54a4-865d-7fbea193d4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-147611" :question/problem "![](images/27/27c1ad7d429eb8da46b0bb3baec048b3564ce206b4523416cb4cb56b0a33767f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6)$, $(0,0),$ $(6,-12).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/9c/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0487d515-4469-551a-b284-54ff67a84fc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e9/e997a8908870618b2aea4d1461c8fd719a4fc1ba0fde1c025a830abeed53aac8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272426} {:answer/id #uuid "25ff1750-b135-5b48-bfe4-4cb0591e5a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd92e2e12164033952a9b4c6233563af86ef6b9add13b66700ab166ff04821a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272720} {:answer/id #uuid "a63a69e5-34c3-529b-92eb-6403b897b096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fee3415af228b80bb5d7c1a68475043fce324234766d243c928fe9eb98e0b900.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273826} {:answer/id #uuid "c04289b2-b02f-5a79-89bd-cc4c2bfd4cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf336b4522756131aeb6dd9bc48ada6f8b255526b6ae20120dcf40f155b1b95c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274050} {:answer/id #uuid "d10fe101-d162-5cd5-9cd5-956d173ec87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/4966000e14a3ed4070b9875848c52ae6a4e3e7d01d15aaf312ae0a2119daf042.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf336b4522756131aeb6dd9bc48ada6f8b255526b6ae20120dcf40f155b1b95c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274050} :answer-field/id #uuid "36eece50-6835-5d1f-9c17-27ce4da964c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274731}] :question/id #uuid "70b24c15-daf3-580d-b9fb-37aeddc79b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-147649" :question/problem "![](images/57/57941a3ed467617de9d41a2d8239b75060ba90b7a8c8980e5dabd3afb0be8b6b.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(-5,5),$ $(-3,3).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/cf/cf336b4522756131aeb6dd9bc48ada6f8b255526b6ae20120dcf40f155b1b95c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b93f461-1c7c-56fa-9e47-cf342c2182e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/40f352980b38be63b071b160953eff23a98996dce58c5f616e10958a8a70182e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288119} {:answer/id #uuid "6d878e48-5182-54e0-9a21-7580d9175240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ee/ee4a96b2b1106fbd1a5ec222c3f7f2a5e5a9e84c9bfe539aeb29a1918943aef9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288798} {:answer/id #uuid "84bcd4c8-95e4-5ba2-812e-8d15253507a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc5ad781e838e597706600633701871006cd59fd3db60344cf34aaddb4200da8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288924} {:answer/id #uuid "bae133f8-955a-587b-8e5f-630c8d7aa03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/92beb71e7d09cba01f2eeb82a60ca3b0b3929064e4f16da3af104db8c5eaa8df.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289265} {:answer/id #uuid "be768ba3-bb22-5082-9403-9396a068e5ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b4/b4d2150d92ff14a654fb7079a17d7bd75abe721c0d37d4075d5a92635bafc170.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ee/ee4a96b2b1106fbd1a5ec222c3f7f2a5e5a9e84c9bfe539aeb29a1918943aef9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288798} :answer-field/id #uuid "9224408d-95cf-5c4a-a8cc-58f66c41fcd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290058}] :question/id #uuid "dcfd5567-90cc-5d33-9aaa-36581e272ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-21063" :question/problem "![](images/65/6501b1a7e9429c786905c11835410111c32ac0337f1ba63bff130d327350316c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(6,3)$, $(8,4)$ and $(10,5).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/a9/a91af151d3dc0e48aef0eef58012f6c9f72aaff02aafae2d55fe0714c29c96e3.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12965d46-110f-51d1-be49-c816e432974f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/461ff9fb5ef66239eb81314f761fac9ceb32b3bc88df6940b61445c752fe3d0c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288163} {:answer/id #uuid "3aac1081-e617-52cc-948d-89da29406dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ed/ed8a2354f8cc04f998875f599a52b50e6c64cafe8976f1bea176772543e295ac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288440} {:answer/id #uuid "430c8598-7cdf-553d-b43a-6da1aef94e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0af059340bdef0548876baad9bcdf990f6bc92330617dde33c18c00578aecad1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288488} {:answer/id #uuid "845c793e-ffa5-5710-b7de-4b57f2fa8dca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da61a7fd99ce683be4e66d3708ddf15c969b038f0250dc4c024ace870c3f7544.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288921} {:answer/id #uuid "8e357473-2063-5ea1-bd53-50d60adebac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf7cc4e728cd1ade741c55b2fbb54720220e0e09a8521a150300532b4e3ee9ed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0af059340bdef0548876baad9bcdf990f6bc92330617dde33c18c00578aecad1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288488} :answer-field/id #uuid "90738e29-17d5-5aba-96ca-bc4630f7480f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290053}] :question/id #uuid "c723b05a-0b3d-5522-bbda-5b3f8ac9a3ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-21065" :question/problem "![](images/db/db7d2b33f2badad28b754d4482047a33bb37469ed8b7b17859b10552840e2f51.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,4)$, \n$(-6,12)$ and $(-1,2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/2e/2e1dde461c6244a59672fc28c842b70a30297ac7a8c7e7cf2095a973cd1860cd.png)"} {:d