 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 20 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,4)$, $(5,20)$, and  $(2,8).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/94/94247512fd446447144d808c76d00bc9c0d50d4175697597360117eca00b3cf1.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49c77e01-4d1d-5c06-a480-d447276bb1d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95fbb1a2298ebc809303d6c57a8440483cdd65748b090ea0b45d25ebad93bb80.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388899} {:answer/id #uuid "b10b56d0-0de6-5d02-bddd-cf895c4147d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f43f19bbe4213ba2f9d5bc51f52b747e1c7840a27607207f0ca56021c1914d5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388900} {:answer/id #uuid "c66d7895-934c-5bb8-97d5-8056fed90107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c688b1ee540e732329e597fb97a0595f619dbc4ff0aad86b6a01f1bdb51ae66b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388901} {:answer/id #uuid "beb8153f-9f67-5cdc-841a-d6318264c4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/37/378a24a8553ac7092b85f715394bf632b5e87aaf45c58ce3ff7ae66310b28f65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388902} {:answer/id #uuid "2e5db3c4-68c8-55f4-9716-051a8b246d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0f0589a467b3d35947a6f501ff00d5296e05ae7e375800659986038db55c7577.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c688b1ee540e732329e597fb97a0595f619dbc4ff0aad86b6a01f1bdb51ae66b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388901} :answer-field/id #uuid "775d1a18-d6fd-53fc-a27b-7894cbc4846a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388898}] :question/id #uuid "babac56b-1bc2-59da-833f-f3070de287aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-147603" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0cec723bf4e6886ca0715e9e02c658a7ee0e1f24555ea3946f95aa2b12b863be.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,2)$, $(-2,2),$ $(2,-2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/c6/c688b1ee540e732329e597fb97a0595f619dbc4ff0aad86b6a01f1bdb51ae66b.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd55c037-00e6-5219-914e-9a5a9bd7534e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e667849ed8a214e7d17871b0f96f73f83c59eec2677bfbaeaab589e04cc89e61.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390404} {:answer/id #uuid "f174cb91-e1ee-5d6c-90ef-6029cbaebf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52266ff97300b29c85ac14f5b60b308d9e8a0e2fe3a01e8e0431b643e6a28922.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390405} {:answer/id #uuid "071cdea1-0dac-5f25-b6f4-63481ba1e33c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1a/1a027e19617c0c62fd8f5247c6d1bbac894f9522ec9e90aec5b7ed05b3996b37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390406} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9aba44-7003-5d32-9bce-752796690c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ca/cac3c2b4fb6191aa9a523b445d8533774f438d24556ea79b8e67a4d6c3867526.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390407} {:answer/id #uuid "38ce622d-f9f2-50a8-99cd-404657278c3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7033ca262624a9723186563638f5ff006d4174a82349be0812ac3de4c25af5e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52266ff97300b29c85ac14f5b60b308d9e8a0e2fe3a01e8e0431b643e6a28922.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390405} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfcca37-0c5f-5e1f-94b7-02dbf414d41e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390403}] :question/id #uuid "f7e170ff-3ef3-51ef-bb76-d32ad791f4a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-21058" :question/problem "![](images/fe/fee79ec0b214a4ba87400b4b8c9dab2c623878d067821c572b26ae241625c48a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 15 & 25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(2,10)$, $(3,15)$, and  $(5,25).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/bf/bf5987fde11416780a6a599e3952db7319e1c0e859e2439b7df70c5659bc6839.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69a5f479-1f02-5295-a376-a3abf036ca37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3b14cd00f6c722d357efc70dd1d7ab68572582a8a916579c575015e2ab52aa3b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395210} {:answer/id #uuid "bf414cc3-d468-5dc2-8a59-1235688ead33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a4fad96436c588fc4285bc037d16b0160894c22aff4c743bc6da7e30382a1bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395211} {:answer/id #uuid "efffb243-6bdd-5da5-9d37-70c237d0ae27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eb5bd61e6c2cc904992d8122682cf972db323d086fbee37c0321ff7746d75a52.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395212} {:answer/id #uuid "09dcccba-e501-5bbf-a9c8-585efd1ffe35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/14c5da55c5f00a409c018dca6bcde6b478f80b6e28a58929fba948d55293de6e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395213} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7b6063-f82b-58a9-983a-2e47106b4d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7a/7a66ac9dd72f2eafa414a80c9c5014740ac5492e27b56e3851019145cf539c4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/14c5da55c5f00a409c018dca6bcde6b478f80b6e28a58929fba948d55293de6e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395213} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f8ce751-7160-534c-b80b-2d02eca7acfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395209}] :question/id #uuid "de81ae6d-990c-555a-8180-3e9f001332f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97021" :question/problem "![](images/67/6724aca14f79c6df70d7bdfca41dc03fb448ae5566d05a5ee9c96dc6cf505812.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,2)$, $(5,-10),$ $(-2,4).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/e7/e7bfe2b85983b2cd45dd3e2f9bbfeed0d8440d838ae11fa4afb0b0b1476529ea.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a113ce26-9b58-57f2-8ce4-5d2801be46ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e3/e3759f48aad9f2b69a76ff0979858e63b464facdad692c75709e989e31c01466.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395217} {:answer/id #uuid "a590d3f8-b473-507a-8d4f-62d36a50c5a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/8218cbbfcd19517e45233cb53649a0daf07cd094defcfd925e9d0b4c48746ccb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395218} {:answer/id #uuid "d00e7780-1fb6-5e01-9c13-82668818b98e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/38/3837eb3e6aaf4ee7fbd5c0d80d588e106d7f13958cd6e9c96dcc8784e8c460e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395219} {:answer/id #uuid "1df1cd66-5d0e-5d8e-bbde-39a748aadefc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aa4ec8c9bbf65797904b60a87f950113b4d720dcce16fc7ace3f349169df83ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395220} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2ccf81-6413-5424-8960-c80f0c98ac13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70d88ffc1ab7dfe2813e73d0106e913d3a1a14975d2d765ebfbd27ff3079eae1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70d88ffc1ab7dfe2813e73d0106e913d3a1a14975d2d765ebfbd27ff3079eae1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395221} :answer-field/id #uuid "624eddbd-0b23-5807-b81a-820e6b2897a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395216}] :question/id #uuid "2ca3fcdf-3fc3-510a-b699-c636d97b2e93" :question/math-academy-id "q-97022" :question/problem "![](images/69/699e6ce441757dd21b01524b5405ab7f4b596bfe9ec6f8d0532a1e6f112eb8ad.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,2)$, $(2,4),$ $(3,6).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/79/791c82648482ef9932562150659ef74bb55df0216047ad56bb84f9bcf1b6ce4d.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of an Object Formed by a Singular Transformation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105895 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105462 :question/id #uuid "4aa087bf-ee6c-5e90-9431-c4be6b207333" :question/math-academy-id "e-12438" :question/problem "![](images/89/89efcd0ecb51dac08a1102c5a347eea3459f7209de7cbac0a88b192259ca3b7e.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](images/50/501ab476f0e420892fee6c87307dd33f260affc1533019621b366b5462920322.png)\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with associated $2 \\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $\\mathbf{T}$ is non-singular, i.e., $\\det(T) \\neq 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $\\mathbf{T}$ is singular, i.e., $\\det(T) = 0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$ is the origin."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fea43b6-fd7b-5edc-b6b7-7f8b2cbab502" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50272988-b890-53f6-a6a1-98aa8ded5b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279324} {:answer/id #uuid "622fb80d-5fba-5d31-9969-daf4c626a166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279483} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1c8d24-5284-5c7d-95c5-1d06ad681c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A point, different from the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280134} {:answer/id #uuid "c71bb996-cc27-596e-bd5d-bc10e4c47114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280337} {:answer/id #uuid "fb282045-7ab5-5935-b512-2d49501f3d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279483} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaa2889d-b25a-5184-a3d7-273fb01be88f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281252}] :question/id #uuid "6dc04420-7edf-5061-a2f1-81e1e58efd27" :question/math-academy-id "q-162145" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-3)-6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a singular nonzero matrix. Therefore, the image of the triangle under the action of $T$ is a line segment."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb34d14-4e6b-5921-bbae-0804ad06b4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102295} {:answer/id #uuid "b2b33753-c1ca-54f2-b9c6-98ba27f6fa8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102296} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1ac350-98a0-5f6c-8490-7f08a97c5de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102297} {:answer/id #uuid "1338e2d6-476a-5cc4-a9f7-69b9fb7f0f6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102298} {:answer/id #uuid "39e1c3d2-cf9c-5c0f-ac61-180359ad5ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A point, different from the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102299}] :answer-field/id #uuid "98d6bd43-1322-57b8-8f87-0e031cdaba61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e72b8eba-d97d-557f-a8cb-b177b5a694e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401317} {:answer/id #uuid "239808c3-6662-5144-b216-bf28876d8c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401318} {:answer/id #uuid "d95c8151-cc29-5467-9bd0-4f7145939834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401319} {:answer/id #uuid "a539e88c-cfb9-5231-b8f6-481fa85848fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401320} {:answer/id #uuid "ace8a67a-e74f-5f27-9582-9a2b3428a829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A point, different from the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401317} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dd41be4-e0dd-5cb0-830a-bc68816c31ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401316}] :question/id #uuid "ba678a53-c013-5d44-b391-2d5cc0a9cc96" :question/math-academy-id "q-162150" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $T$ is the origin."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148840cb-8cea-5745-9f92-680dd7f0ea95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278774} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb3d88b-4028-5ec9-80c5-a2ea9fc98832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A point, different from the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279438} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7deda2-0f82-5af4-aed7-d429a9518b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280104} {:answer/id #uuid "b4822b66-d6bb-592a-a36a-a168beb56876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280182} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ad46d1-cb7b-5e5e-844d-6c83af425320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A quadrilateral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A quadrilateral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280215} :answer-field/id #uuid "47cd30e7-fd7a-5e03-89d2-7a44f08b81a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280953}] :question/id #uuid "0f03e3e5-8f9e-5206-8323-aab2c0298778" :question/math-academy-id "q-162206" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e6d0ce147aec90c3840a893e36596fbadf981ff96559f65d055f4486406cca7f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a nonsingular matrix. Therefore, the image of our object under the action of  $T$ is a quadrilateral."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a6e4373-347b-586f-904c-be59818f4945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279110} {:answer/id #uuid "5d56f302-e7a0-5f70-b0e0-272d1328de15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A pentagon" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279448} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf17246-a02f-5adb-adca-449dd47e93a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A point, different from the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280536} {:answer/id #uuid "e92272a3-0f88-52d3-9b2f-9e2c60c5273f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280642} {:answer/id #uuid "f3652a9c-788f-5fa8-a9ee-b638c4ee6bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279110} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4f360b7-8b35-5cc3-a7cb-82ef205491ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281270}] :question/id #uuid "0a4d15c5-f7e2-5db8